[?2004hroot@c9c9da0bf7e7:/task# nl -ba /task/input/part_A/screen_sop.md
[?2004l     1	# SOP FG-017: pooled CRISPR drug-modifier screens, analysis and release (rev. 4)
     2	
     3	## 1. Scope
     4	Secondary (validation) knockout screens with a T0 reference, a vehicle arm and a drug arm. This
     5	SOP states what a released analysis has to satisfy. It does not prescribe software.
     6	
     7	## 2. Library annotation
     8	Only the current release of a library annotation is used. For VAL-2 this is release 2
     9	(`library.tsv`). Release 2 corrected the gene assignment of 80 sgRNAs (20 genes) that
    10	were mislabelled in release 1 (a sub-pool of the oligo order sheet was shifted against its gene
    11	column); sgRNA ids and sequences did not change. Release 1 is withdrawn.
    12	
    13	## 3. Counting and sample identity
    14	- A read is counted for an sgRNA if it carries that sgRNA's spacer in the amplicon context
    15	  described in the wet-lab notes. Every library of the sample sheet is counted and reported.
    16	- The sample sheet is what the wet lab wrote down. Before any contrast is computed, the arm of
    17	  every day-14 library is confirmed from the data: the sgRNA profile of a library has to agree
    18	  better with the other libraries of its arm than with the libraries of the other arm. A library
    19	  that does not is analysed in the arm its profile supports. The arm in which each library was
    20	  analysed is recorded in `qc.json`.
    21	
    22	## 4. Scales
    23	Log2 fold changes are reported on the scale on which the non-targeting sgRNAs do not change
    24	(median non-targeting sgRNA = 0). The fitness effect is vehicle day 14 against T0. The drug effect
    25	is drug day 14 against vehicle day 14; negative values mean depletion under drug.
    26	
    27	## 5. Release criterion for modifier calls
    28	The library carries reference genes for the compound class (`reference_genes.tsv`): modifiers with
    29	their expected class and genes established not to modify the response (`none`); the reference
    30	`none` genes cover the whole range of fitness effects. A call set is released only if
    31	- at least 9 of the 10 reference modifiers are called with their expected class, and
    32	- at most 1 of the 30 reference `none` genes is called (either class).
    33	The reference genes are reported like every other gene.
    34	
    35	## 6. Hand-over audit checklist
    36	When a project changes hands, the new analyst checks the inherited files and records one verdict
    37	per item in `audit.tsv`: `ok` if the statement holds, `defective` if it does not. Each item is
    38	judged on its own: an effect that follows from the defect of another item is recorded under the
    39	item that caused it, not under every item it touches.
    40	
    41	| item | statement |
    42	|---|---|
    43	| `library_release` | The sgRNA-to-gene annotation in the inherited count table is that of the current library release. |
    44	| `sample_columns` | No sample column of the inherited count table was counted from a FASTQ file other than the one the sample sheet lists for that sample. (A column without any counts is the subject of `read2_library`, not of this item.) |
    45	| `stagger_reads` | The inherited count table contains the reads of all stagger variants of the amplicon, not only of one read layout. |
    46	| `read2_library` | The library that was delivered as Read 2 has been counted: no sample column of the inherited count table is empty. |
    47	| `arm_labels` | The inherited analysis script takes the arm of each library from the sample sheet; every library is thereby analysed in the arm of the treatment it actually received. |
    48	| `control_normalisation` | The inherited analysis script reports log2 fold changes on the scale of section 4 (non-targeting sgRNAs at 0). |
    49	| `drug_baseline` | The drug effect in the inherited analysis script compares the drug arm with the vehicle arm of day 14, not with T0. |
    50	| `contrast_sign` | In the inherited analysis script a negative drug effect means depletion under drug. |
    51	
    52	The inherited gene table and hit list are the output of the inherited analysis script run on the
    53	inherited count table with the sample sheet.
    54	
    55	## 7. Erratum
    56	If results have left the facility, an erratum lists every gene of the mailed list with one verdict:
    57	`confirmed` if the gene is a modifier (either class) in the released analysis, `retracted` if not.
